# demo_flow

> Scaffolded by `flows new --profile web --tier a`. Modeled on `examples/s1_echo`.

## Story

TODO: describe what this flow proves — the user/operator story, the route it
exposes, and any bindings it will need once the placeholder logic is replaced.

This tier-a scaffold ships a minimal honest Web flow:

- one HTTP trigger node (`trigger`)
- one Pure transform node (`process`)
- one responder/capture node (`responder`)
- route alias `POST /demo-flow`

Authoring conventions: `impl-docs/spec/example-authoring-conventions.md`.

## Verify (tier a)

Run from the workspace root. `<this-crate-dir>` is the directory this README
lives in.

```sh
# 1. Compile the crate.
cargo check -p example-demo-flow

# 2. Validate the Flow IR graph (topology, effects, determinism).
cargo run -q -p example-demo-flow --bin dump_ir | flows graph check

# 3. Validate trigger/capture entrypoint wiring.
cargo run -q -p example-demo-flow --bin dump_ir > /tmp/demo_flow.ir.json
flows entrypoints check \
  --flow /tmp/demo_flow.ir.json \
  --trigger-alias trigger \
  --capture-alias responder

# 4. Run locally against the sample payload (after registering in the CLI;
#    see "Serving via the CLI" below).
flows run local --example demo_flow \
  --payload-file <this-crate-dir>/payloads/sample.json
```

> `flows` is the `flows-cli` binary: `cargo run -p flows-cli --bin flows -- ...`,
> or install it and call `flows` directly.

## Serving via the CLI

`flows run local --example demo_flow` and `flows run serve --example
demo_flow` require a manual registration step (the built-in example registry
is still hand-maintained):

1. Add a path dependency on `example-demo-flow` to `crates/cli/Cargo.toml`.
2. Add `use example_demo_flow as demo_flow;` near the other
   `use example_*` imports in `crates/cli/src/main.rs`.
3. Add a match arm to `load_example(...)` in `crates/cli/src/main.rs`:
   `"demo_flow" => (demo_flow::bundle(), false),`

Until then, steps 1–3 above (`cargo check`, `graph check`, `entrypoints check`)
verify the flow without registration.
